## GitHub Issues

All 6 problems have been filed as separate issues in the public triage repo:

- [Issue #1: Wrong Day of Week on Invite](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/1)
- [Issue #2: Month and Day Swapped in Locale Format](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/2)
- [Issue #3: Booking Date Mismatch Between UI and Invite](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/3)
- [Issue #4: Appointment Auto-Moved Without User Action](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/4)
- [Issue #5: Reminder Sent on Wrong Date](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/5)
- [Issue #6: Generic Date/Time Issues (Triage Required)](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/6)

## Lessons

- A merged ticket that looks like one issue often contains multiple independent bugs.
- Locale-aware date handling requires consistent application across all systems (booking, invite, reminder, display).
- A 32% "other" category is a signal to continue triage, not a reason to stop.
- Categorization requires reading individual reports, not just subject lines.

